{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED. Change 1715 merged to main as **641ba8bed1** (\"Split event_append by concern into three modules\") at `LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1`; Gerrit rebased server-side (patchset 3) and submitted.\n\nFinal landed state on main:\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — **524** LOC (from 743; **276** of cap headroom). Retains the locked write transaction (the three `lock.write_lock` bodies, batch rollback, push / enrich-drain hand-off) plus the commit-failure self-heal.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` — **145** LOC, NEW leaf. Pre-lock validation, canonical serialisation, staging hand-off.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py` — **183** LOC, NEW leaf. The bounded git verbs every lock-held git child is issued through.\n\nNo file in `src/rebar` exceeds 800. All five moved regions byte-identical; both new modules leaf-verified by AST; zero test edits; all bindings preserved via redundant-alias re-exports (including the alias-only `canonical_bytes` the plan reviewer caught).\n\n**The `Verified -1` on patchset 1 was proven pre-existing.** Control experiment: the identical single failure (`test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`) reproduces on pristine `origin/main` with this change absent — 1 failed, 12691 passed, in a separate worktree with its own venv resolving `rebar` to that tree. Root cause and a one-line fix (pin `caplog.at_level` on the originating logger, per the 9ac2 precedent already applied in the sibling 2b16 file) are filed on bug `fanatical-skittish-stud`; out of scope here.\n\nPatchset 2 was a full re-derivation of the split, because `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle` (change 1713, c8a380e24c) landed mid-flight and rewrote the exact region being extracted — moving the transient-retry family into the shared `gitutil` seam. `gitutil.py` itself was not touched by this change.\n\nAll acceptance criteria met and ticked. Closing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786614282618639001,"uuid":"fd8453f3-9bab-49ed-a809-da46b97d7b61"}